[S6 forward forgery / other device body (B>C)] stage=2 => STATE_TPM_COUNTER_MISMATCH
[S7 body without certify at matching counter] stage=1 => STATE_TPM_ATTEST_INVALID (certify absent)
[S8 unparseable manifest] stage=1 => STATE_TPM_ATTEST_INVALID (manifest unparseable)
[S9 retired device booted] stage=3 => STATE_RETIRED
[S10 retired + halted both set] stage=3 => STATE_HALT_SOVEREIGN (AMBIGUOUS: halted&&retired both true — matrix lists two matching rows; priority not stated)
[S11 retirement seal torn between increment and commit on OLD device (B_pre=C-1)] stage=2 => STATE_MANIFEST_TPM_TORN (C==B+1 (no idle completion))
NOTE S11: old device is TORN (not RETIRED). TORN is resumable by the sovereign resume path (§د الاستئناف); the matrix has no input representing an issued-but-uncommitted retirement record, so "retired row prevents dual running" holds only if the retirement commit succeeded.
NOTE resume: the only halted→running transition is the sovereign resume path, which is outside the matrix inputs; its binding to the specific halt (counter/digest) is not specified in §د/§ج.
